- 500 total DB items (items 1–50 → hot, others → cold)
- Each client has a cache of 100 items (LRU replacement)
- Requests are generated every `T_query` seconds (mean)
- Updates arrive every `T_update` seconds (mean), only to hot items
- Upon cache hit, client sends a **`check` message** to the server to verify validity
- If valid → return data from cache; otherwise, invalid -> fetch fresh data
- Server responds with either the requested data or confirmation (`confirm`)
