Here's a simple, well-commented C program that calculates the dimensions for a **Biquad antenna with a reflector** — commonly used in WiFi (2.4 GHz or 5 GHz) applications. This program computes:

- The **side length (S)** of the square biquad loop
- The **feed gap (G)** between the two ends of the biquad
- The **reflector spacing (D)** from the biquad
- The **reflector size (R)** (same as biquad side length)

> ✅ **Designed for:**
> - Center frequency: `f` in MHz
> - Speed of light: `c ≈ 3e8 m/s`
> - Uses the **standard Biquad formula** with a velocity factor (~0.95 for typical wire)

---

### ✅ Biquad Antenna Calculator (C Code)

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <math.h>

// Constants
#define SPEED_OF_LIGHT 299792458.0  // m/s
#define VELOCITY_FACTOR 0.95        // Approximate for copper wire

// Function to convert MHz to meters for wavelength
double wavelength(double freq_mhz) {
    return (SPEED_OF_LIGHT / (freq_mhz * 1e6)) * VELOCITY_FACTOR;
}

// Main function
int main() {
    double freq_mhz;        // Operating frequency in MHz (e.g., 2450 for 2.45 GHz)
    double lambda;          // Wavelength (meters)
    double S, G, D, R;      // Dimensions in meters

    printf("=== Biquad Antenna with Reflector Calculator ===\n");
    printf("Enter operating frequency (MHz): ");
    scanf("%lf", &freq_mhz);

    if (freq_mhz <= 0) {
        printf("Error: Frequency must be positive.\n");
        return 1;
    }

    // Calculate effective wavelength
    lambda = wavelength(freq_mhz);

    // Biquad loop side length (S): ~λ/2 (for half-wave biquad)
    S = lambda / 2.0;

    // Feed gap (G): typically 0.005 to 0.01 λ
    G = lambda * 0.007;  // 0.7% of wavelength → good balance

    // Reflector spacing (D): typically λ/4
    D = lambda / 4.0;

    // Reflector size (R): same as biquad side
    R = S;

    // Output results
    printf("\n=== Calculated Dimensions (in meters) ===\n");
    printf("Frequency:         %.2f MHz\n", freq_mhz);
    printf("Wavelength (λ):    %.4f m\n", lambda);
    printf("Biquad side (S):   %.4f m  (%.2f cm)\n", S, S * 100);
    printf("Feed gap (G):      %.4f m  (%.2f cm)\n", G, G * 100);
    printf("Reflector spacing (D): %.4f m  (%.2f cm)\n", D, D * 100);
    printf("Reflector size (R): %.4f m  (%.2f cm)\n", R, R * 100);

    // Suggested material
    printf("\n=== Design Notes ===\n");
    printf("• Use copper wire or aluminum sheet for biquad.\n");
    printf("• Reflector: Flat metal sheet (e.g., aluminum) larger than R.\n");
    printf("• Feed point: Center of the gap (G), use 50Ω coaxial cable (e.g., RG-58).\n");
    printf("• Mount biquad 1–2 cm above reflector for optimal gain.\n");

    return 0;
}
```

