### ✅ Step-by-Step Implementation:

#### 🔹 3.1 Define a Modular, Serializable Task Interface

```java
// Task.java
import java.io.Serializable;

public interface Task<T> extends Serializable {
    T execute();
}
```

> This allows any computationally heavy operation (e.g., matrix multiplication, image filtering, Monte Carlo simulation) to be turned into a callable task.

#### 🔹 3.2 Example Concrete Task

```java
// PrimeCountTask.java
public class PrimeCountTask implements Task<Integer> {
    private final int start;
    private final int end;

    public PrimeCountTask(int start, int end) {
        this.start = start;
        this.end = end;
    }

    @Override
    public Integer execute() {
        int count = 0;
        for (int i = start; i <= end; i++) {
            if (isPrime(i)) count++;
        }
        return count;
    }

    private boolean isPrime(int n) {
        if (n < 2) return false;
        if (n == 2) return true;
        if (n % 2 == 0) return false;
        for (int i = 3; i * i <= n; i += 2)
            if (n % i == 0) return false;
        return true;
    }

    // For debugging/logging
    public String toString() {
        return "PrimeCountTask{" + start + "–" + end + "}";
    }
}
```

