## 🔷 Step 4: Use `ExecutorService` or `ForkJoinPool` on Both Devices to Process Tasks

Now let’s set up **parallel execution** on both ends.

---

### ✅ On Desktop PC: Use `ExecutorService` for High-Throughput Local Processing

Already implemented in `TaskManager.java` above.

```java
private static final ExecutorService WORKER_POOL = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(4);
```

This leverages **CPU affinity**, avoiding context switching overhead.

Use:
- `CompletableFuture` for chaining
- `ForkJoinPool` if tasks are recursive/divisible (like divide-and-conquer algorithms)

#### 🔸 When to Use `ForkJoinPool`
If your problem is inherently **recursive**, like tree traversal or merge sort:

```java
public class ParallelMergeSortTask implements RecursiveTask<int[]> {
    private final int[] array;
    private final int start, end;

    public ParallelMergeSortTask(int[] array, int start, int end) {
        this.array = array;
        this.start = start;
        this.end = end;
    }

    @Override
    protected int[] compute() {
        if (end - start < 1000) { // Base case: small enough to sort locally
            Arrays.sort(array, start, end);
            return Arrays.copyOfRange(array, start, end);
        }

        int mid = (start + end) / 2;
        ForkJoinTask<int[]> left = new ParallelMergeSortTask(array, start, mid).fork();
        int[] right = new ParallelMergeSortTask(array, mid, end).compute();
        int[] leftResult = left.join();
        return merge(leftResult, right);
    }
}
```

Then in `TaskManager`:
```java
ForkJoinPool pool = new ForkJoinPool();
pool.invoke(new ParallelMergeSortTask(data, 0, data.length));
```

Use `ForkJoinPool` for **intra-task recursion** on each device.

---

### ✅ On Android Device: Implement Worker Service Using `ExecutorService`

Create a **background service** that listens for incoming tasks:

```java
// AndroidWorkerService.java (in Android app)
public class AndroidWorkerService extends Service {
    private volatile boolean running = true;
    private ExecutorService executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(
        Runtime.getRuntime().availableProcessors()
    );

    @Override
    public int onStartCommand(Intent intent, int flags, int startId) {
        new Thread(this::runListenerLoop).start();
        return START_STICKY;
    }

    private void runListenerLoop() {
        try (ServerSocket serverSocket = new ServerSocket(8080)) {
            System.out.println("📱 Android Worker waiting for tasks on port 8080");

            while (running) {
                try (Socket clientSocket = serverSocket.accept();
                     ObjectInputStream in = new ObjectInputStream(clientSocket.getInputStream());
                     ObjectOutputStream out = new ObjectOutputStream(clientSocket.getOutputStream())) {

                    List<Task<?>> tasks = (List<Task<?>>) in.readObject();
                    System.out.println("📥 Received " + tasks.size() + " tasks.");

                    List<Object> results = new ArrayList<>();
                    for (Task<?> task : tasks) {
                        try {
                            results.add(task.execute());
                        } catch (Exception e) {
                            e.printStackTrace();
                            results.add(null);
                        }
                    }

                    out.writeObject(results);
                    out.flush();
                } catch (IOException | ClassNotFoundException e) {
                    if (!running) break;
                    e.printStackTrace();
                }
            }
        } catch (IOException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }

    @Override
    public void onDestroy() {
        running = false;
        executor.shutdown();
        super.onDestroy();
    }

    @Nullable
    @Override
    public IBinder onBind(Intent intent) {
        return null;
    }
}
```

Register in `AndroidManifest.xml`:

```xml
<service android:name=".AndroidWorkerService"
         android:exported="true"
         android:permission="android.permission.INTERNET">
    <intent-filter>
        <action android:name="android.intent.action.MAIN"/>
    </intent-filter>
</service>
```

Also add:
```xml
