You're building a fun little game (Sobics) and now want to **save the player's score and name to a text file when the game ends**, using **only HTML, CSS, and JavaScript (no backend)**.

But there's a critical limitation:

> 🚫 **You cannot directly write to a file on a user's computer using standard JavaScript in a browser**, because of security restrictions. Browsers **do not allow direct file system access** for security reasons.

---

### ✅ Solution: Simulate "saving" with **File Download** (Client-Side Only)

Instead of writing directly to a file, we'll **generate a `.txt` file and trigger a download** with the score and name.

This is the closest you can get to "saving to a file" using just client-side code.

---

## ✅ Step-by-Step Implementation

### ✅ 1. Add a "Toplist" Modal (Pop-up) When Game Ends

We’ll create a modal where the player can enter their name, then trigger a download.

---

### ✅ 2. Update `endGame()` Function

Replace your current `endGame()` function with this improved version:

```javascript
function endGame() {
  document.removeEventListener("mousemove", dragRectangle);
  backgroundMusic.pause();

  // Stop the game from progressing
  clearTimeout(timeoutId); // if you had a timer stored

  // Show the toplist form
  const toplistModal = document.createElement('div');
  toplistModal.style.position = 'fixed';
  toplistModal.style.top = '50%';
  toplistModal.style.left = '50%';
  toplistModal.style.transform = 'translate(-50%, -50%)';
  toplistModal.style.backgroundColor = '#fff';
  toplistModal.style.padding = '30px';
  toplistModal.style.borderRadius = '10px';
  toplistModal.style.boxShadow = '0 0 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.5)';
  toplistModal.style.zIndex = '1000';
  toplistModal.style.width = '300px';
  toplistModal.style.textAlign = 'center';

  toplistModal.innerHTML = `
    <h2>🎉 Game Over!</h2>
    <p>Your score: <strong>${score}</strong></p>
    <label for="playerName">Enter your name:</label>
    <input type="text" id="playerName" placeholder="Your Name" style="margin: 10px; padding: 8px; width: 80%;" maxlength="20">
    <button onclick="saveToToplist()" style="margin-top: 10px; padding: 10px 20px; background-color: #1c9e6c; color: white; border: none; border-radius: 5px; cursor: pointer;">
      Save to Toplist
    </button>
  `;

  document.body.appendChild(toplistModal);

  // Focus the input
  document.getElementById("playerName").focus();

  // Optional: Add escape key to close
  document.addEventListener("keydown", function closeOnEscape(e) {
    if (e.key === "Escape") {
      document.body.removeChild(toplistModal);
      document.removeEventListener("keydown", closeOnEscape);
    }
  });
}
```

---

### ✅ 3. Add `saveToToplist()` Function

This is the main function that creates a `.txt` file and triggers a download.

```javascript
function saveToToplist() {
  const playerNameInput = document.getElementById("playerName");
  const name = playerNameInput.value.trim() || "Anonymous";

  const scoreText = `Name: ${name} | Score: ${score}`;

  // Create Blob (file-like object)
  const blob = new Blob([scoreText], { type: 'text/plain' });

  // Create download link
  const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
  const a = document.createElement('a');
  a.href = url;
  a.download = 'toplist.txt'; // filename
  a.style.display = 'none';
  document.body.appendChild(a);
  a.click();

  // Clean up
  setTimeout(() => {
    document.body.removeChild(a);
    URL.revokeObjectURL(url);
  }, 100);

  // Remove modal
  const modal = document.querySelector('#toplistModal');
  if (modal) {
    document.body.removeChild(modal);
  }

  // Optional: Reset game
  // You can re-enable startGame() etc.
  alert("Toplist saved as 'toplist.txt'! Check your downloads folder.");
}
```

> 💡 You must **add `id="toplistModal"`** to the modal element in `endGame()` for cleanup, or just use a `querySelector` like this:  
> ```js
> const modal = document.querySelector('div[style*="position: fixed"]');
> ```

But to make it safe, we’ll slightly revise the `endGame()` function to give the modal an ID:

```javascript
// Inside endGame(), replace this line:
const toplistModal = document.createElement('div');
toplistModal.id = 'toplistModal'; // Add this ID
```

Now `saveToToplist()` can safely remove it.

