## 🚀 How to Deploy to GitHub Pages

1. Push your code to a new GitHub repository:
   ```bash
   git init
   git add .
   git commit -m "Initial commit"
   git branch -M main
   git remote add origin https://github.com/yourusername/blog-website.git
   git push -u origin main
   ```

2. Go to GitHub repository settings → Pages → Choose "gh-pages" branch → Deploy.

3. In the GitHub repository, create a file `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` to automate deployment:
   ```yaml
   name: Deploy to GitHub Pages

   on:
     push:
       branches: [ main ]

   jobs:
     deploy:
       runs-on: ubuntu-latest
       steps:
         - uses: actions/checkout@v3
           with:
             submodules: true

         - name: Setup Node.js
           uses: actions/setup-node@v3
           with:
             node-version: 18

         - name: Install dependencies
           run: npm install

         - name: Build
           run: npm run build

         - name: Export
           run: npm run export

         - name: Deploy
           uses: peaceiris/actions-gh-pages@v3
           with:
             github_token: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
             publish_dir: ./out
   ```

4. The blog will now be available at: `https://yourusername.github.io/blog-website`

