## ✅ **Case 2: Product Order Form with Discount Logic**

### 🎯 **Objective**:  
Create a simple product order form that accepts a list of items and quantities. Apply discounts based on total quantity. Display cart and calculate final price.

---

### ✅ **File: `order_form.php`**

```php
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>🛒 Product Order Form</title>
    <style>
        body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; margin: 30px; }
        .form-group { margin: 15px 0; }
        label { display: inline-block; width: 130px; }
        input[type="text"], input[type="number"] { width: 100px; padding: 5px; }
        button { padding: 10px; background: #28a745; color: white; border: none; cursor: pointer; }
        .cart { margin-top: 20px; padding: 15px; background: #f8f9fa; border: 1px solid #ddd; }
        .cart h4 { margin-top: 0; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<h2>🛒 Order Your Products</h2>

<form method="POST" action="">
    <h3>Add Products</h3>
    <?php
    $products = [
        'Laptop' => 999,
        'Mouse' => 25,
        'Keyboard' => 75,
        'Monitor' => 300,
        'Headphones' => 150
    ];
    $items = $_POST['items'] ?? [];
    ?>

    <?php foreach ($products as $name => $price): ?>
        <div class="form-group">
            <label><?= htmlspecialchars($name) ?>:</label>
            <input type="number" name="items[<?= $name ?>]" value="<?= htmlspecialchars($items[$name] ?? 0) ?>" min="0" max="10">
            <span style="color:gray;">(Price: $<?= number_format($price, 2) ?>)</span>
        </div>
    <?php endforeach; ?>

    <button type="submit" name="submit">Add to Cart</button>
</form>

<?php
// Process order
if (isset($_POST['submit'])) {
    $items = $_POST['items'] ?? [];
    $total = 0;
    $totalItems = 0;
    $cartItems = [];

    // Use For loop to check items and calculate
    for ($i = 0; $i < count($items); $i++) {
        $productNames = array_keys($items);
        $itemName = $productNames[$i];
        $qty = $items[$itemName];

        if ($qty > 0) {
            $price = $products[$itemName];
            $itemTotal = $price * $qty;
            $total += $itemTotal;
            $totalItems += $qty;

            $cartItems[] = [
                'name' => $itemName,
                'qty' => $qty,
                'price' => $price,
                'total' => $itemTotal
            ];
        }
    }

    // Use conditionals and operators for discount
    $discount = 0;
    if ($totalItems >= 5) {
        $discount = $total * 0.1; // 10% off
    } elseif ($totalItems >= 3) {
        $discount = $total * 0.05; // 5% off
    }

    $finalTotal = $total - $discount;

    // Use a while loop to display cart
    echo "<div class='cart'>";
    echo "<h4>Your Cart:</h4>";
    echo "<ul>";

    $i = 0;
    while ($i < count($cartItems)) {
        $item = $cartItems[$i];
        echo "<li><strong>{$item['name']}</strong>: {$item['qty']} × \${$item['price']} = \${$item['total']}</li>";
        $i++;
    }
    echo "</ul>";

    echo "<p><strong>Subtotal:</strong> \${$total}</p>";
    if ($discount > 0) {
        echo "<p><strong>Discount ({$discount > 0 ? '10%' : '5%'}):</strong> -\${number_format($discount, 2)}</p>";
    }
    echo "<p><strong>Final Total:</strong> \${number_format($finalTotal, 2)}</p>";
    echo "</div>";
}
?>

</body>
</html>
```

